{% doc %}
  "Find your size" sheet (redesign 2026-11-14, mockup SizeSheet.dc.html).
  Full-screen sheet on phones, centred dialog on desktop. Opened by any
  element with data-pt-size-sheet (results header Change size / Find your
  size, the filter drawer's Find your size, the home hero, the header search
  overlay). Every trigger is a real link or button that still works when this
  script does not load (the link goes to the Shop by size hub, the results
  header button opens the old size panel).

  This snippet only prints the config and loads the assets; the sheet's DOM is
  built by assets/pt-size-sheet.js the first time it opens.

  Data (nothing invented):
  - Width / aspect / rim options: assets/pt-tire-sizes.json, the size index
    the home search already uses (sizes we carry). If it cannot load, the
    same fixed lists the results-page size dropdowns use.
  - Vehicle: pt-vehicle-manifest.json + pt-vehicle-<year>.json (same as
    every vehicle search), resolving to the trim's tire sizes; a staggered
    trim's front + rear sets via assets/pt-vehicle-pairs.js (loaded here).
  - "Show N tires": sections/pt-rd-count rendered for the destination URL
    (Section Rendering API). No count -> "Show tires".
  - Pick up where you left off: localStorage pt-recent-searches (shared
    search history), pt-garage-<customer.id> (the signed-in customer's own
    My Garage default car; nothing for guests), pt-tire-search-vehicle (last
    vehicle searched).
  - Layout (owner 2026-11-14): a "Type your size" box (any common format;
    a typo or a size we don't stock gets a plain message, never the whole
    catalogue under that size's name), small "Recent" chips, then width /
    aspect / rim as three dropdowns side by side, season once complete.

  Rendered once from sections/pt-header.liquid (every page).

  @example
    {% render 'pt-size-sheet' %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign pss_min_year = settings.smart_search_min_year | default: 2001
  assign pss_max_year = settings.smart_search_max_year | default: 2026
  assign pss_vehicle_url = 'pt-vehicle-2025.json' | asset_url
  assign pss_vehicle_base = pss_vehicle_url | split: 'pt-vehicle-2025.json' | first
  assign pss_vehicle_ver = ''
  if pss_vehicle_url contains '?'
    assign pss_vehicle_ver = pss_vehicle_url | split: '?' | last
  endif
-%}
{% render 'pt-vehicle-manifest-loader' %}
{% render 'pt-search-tracking' %}
<script type="application/json" id="pt-size-sheet-config">
{
  "sizesUrl": {{ 'pt-tire-sizes.json' | asset_url | json }},
  "manifestUrl": {{ 'pt-vehicle-manifest.json' | asset_url | json }},
  "vehicleBase": {{ pss_vehicle_base | json }},
  "vehicleVersion": {{ pss_vehicle_ver | json }},
  "minYear": {{ pss_min_year | json }},
  "maxYear": {{ pss_max_year | json }},
  "tiresUrl": {{ routes.collections_url | append: '/tires' | json }},
  "hubUrl": {{ routes.collections_url | append: '/all' | json }},
  "customerId": {% if customer %}{{ customer.id | json }}{% else %}null{% endif %}
}
</script>
{%- comment -%} Not render-blocking: the sheet only exists after a tap. {%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'pt-size-sheet.css' | asset_url }}" media="print" onload="this.media='all'" data-pss-css><script src="{{ 'pt-size-sheet.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- comment -%} Front + rear sets for a staggered trim on EVERY page (product pages, /pages/*), not only where the grid / hero / tire search load it. The helper ignores a second copy (if (P.lookup) return). {%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'pt-vehicle-pairs.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
